    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d803">

                <pb facs="0916" n="814" xml:id="pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/599: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-07T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1919, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 5, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>Second paragraph not entirely clear to Department. Cannot Nicaraguan Government,
                    under existing appropriations, send sufficient forces to frontier to police it,
                    if not, what is the “proper authority required.”</p>
                <p>In your opinion would the sending of Nicaraguan troops to the frontier meet the
                    needs of the present situation as expressed in Department’s May 3, 4 p.m. or
                    would such action arouse suspicions of Costa Rica and be provocative of
                    trouble.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
